  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Combinations in Real Life 2 - Livestock and shamba selections</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) A farmer in Kakamega has \({@pn1@}\) goats and wants to take \({@pr1@}\) of them to the market to sell. In how many ways can the farmer choose which goats to take?</p>
<p>Number of ways = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) A family has \({@pn2@}\) different crops they could plant (such as maize, beans, sukuma wiki, tomatoes and onions) but have room in their shamba for only \({@pr2@}\) different crops. How many different groups of crops can they choose?</p>
<p>Number of groups = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>The order in which the goats are chosen does not matter, so this is \(_{ {@pn1@} }C_{ {@pr1@} }\). Choosing which \({@pr1@}\) goats to sell is the same as choosing which \({@pn1-pr1@}\) goats to keep, so \(_{ {@pn1@} }C_{ {@pr1@} } = {}_{ {@pn1@} }C_{ {@pn1-pr1@} }\):</p>
<p>\(_{ {@pn1@} }C_{ {@pr1@} } = \dfrac{ {@pn1@}!}{ {@pr1@}!\,{@pn1-pr1@}!} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p>For part (b), planting maize and beans is the same as planting beans and maize, so this is \(_{ {@pn2@} }C_{ {@pr2@} }\):</p>
<p>\(_{ {@pn2@} }C_{ {@pr2@} } = \dfrac{ {@pn2@}!}{ {@pr2@}!\,{@pn2-pr2@}!} = {@ta2@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
